That's how all tags are defined in the Lojban-Lojban section of jbovlaste, yes.

> Anyway, is {fa'a} {fi'o farna} or {fi'o se farna}? I'd be inclined to say
> {fi'o *se* farna} seeing as I honestly have no clue what one might put in
> farna1...

It's "fi'o farna". The sumti indicates the point towards which the
event is oriented. For example "fa'a lo gapru" for "upwards".

Most other FAhA's however do correspond to a SE-converted gismu.

